WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.405
Weeds, pests and diseases can cut your harvest. Spot them early.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:10.591
Weeds take light, water and food from your cassava. Weed early and often while plants are young.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:15.265
Cassava mosaic disease makes leaves yellow, spotted and twisted.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:20.907
Remove and destroy badly affected plants. Never use their stems for planting.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:27.907
Mealybugs and green mites are small insects on leaves and shoot tips, more common in the dry season.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:34.466
If many plants are affected, ask your local agricultural extension officer for advice.

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:43.124
Before you move on, check: Weed while plants are young. Learn the signs of mosaic disease. Know your extension officer.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:47.217
In the next lesson: When and how to harvest.
